{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start","id":954864,"title":"Things you wish you knew from the start.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-08-21T00:04:12-07:00","id":954864,"title":"Things you wish you knew from the start.","content":"Hi everyone. This is just a general thread I thought I would like to start. I've seen a few threads of new storytellers asking for advice on whatever adventure they are beginning. I myself have asked a few times and am sure that there are a lot of little tips and tricks that more experienced storytellers have learned in their journeys. So, any and all storytellers, I invite you to pass some words of wisdom that may not be so obvious to someone new to the scene, that you wished you had known when you first started out.<br /> <br /> For example. I like having essentially a random encounter/event sheet prepared for the setting. If the characters are in an area that I didn't really have anything planned, I can just roll a die and a variety of things may occur. These events changed based off of what game is being run, but same principle applies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3268,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","user":"Krzyzstof","date":". 08-21-2016, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T02:10:27-07:00","id":954892,"title":"","content":"NPCs don't need full character sheets, just a handful of likely dice rolls. Hired goons probably have Shoot The Heroes (Four Dice) and Run Away (Six Dice), with five Health and a 2 in everything else. Doing things that way really cuts down on bookkeeping and speeds up play.<br /> <br /> I also wish I'd been more strongly discouraged from crossover play, as it leads to a lot if headache unless everyone is much more experienced with CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T05:16:20-07:00","id":954910,"title":"","content":"Have a story to tell.<br /> <br /> Have a goal in mind when you sit down to run a campaign. I set vague limits for how long a story should be, which then influences how much direct exposition I give or not, how long the downtime scenes should be, if I should cut to a montage, and trim the setting to something we can all wrap our heads around without diluting themes.<br /> <br /> Don't build a world. Build a home.<br /> <br /> Half reiterated from a post I made recently on the Werewolf forum, but your campaign can continue past epic threats. Killing the Idigam means you saved the day but guess what? There's more days, and just like real life they can be boring. They can go back to normal...except in the Chronicles of Darkness 'normal' means the Pure attack your turf, your ex-wife is possessed by a ghost, and a creepy clown is stealing the faces of children. Show what happens <i>after</i> the story ends. Life goes on, the world keeps spinning.<br /> <br /> Antagonists threaten their home. Your characters live here. They have friends and family. They have regrets. They have things they forgot about that they wish they could remember and experience one more time. They have an imagined life that they thought would go a little differently; not as in, &quot;I wish I didn't become a vampire&quot; but more, &quot;I wish I told her how much I loved her before she left me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T18:36:02-07:00","id":955342,"title":"","content":"I wish someone had told me this was a horror game. Or my players.<br /> <br /> Or had generally convinced me <i>not</i> to run a game where the guy who thought he was Robin Hood was the character that made the most sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T20:49:11-07:00","id":955393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=955342#post955342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wish someone had told me this was a horror game. Or my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is essential. A lot of people come at these games with an urban fantasy mindset and the rules are going to fight them every step of the way, leading to a lot of suffering at the table and angry forum posts later. Being upfront about how every line is going to try its darndest to hammer home both personal horror and its unique themes is really going to help things along.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T22:16:42-07:00","id":955434,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=955393#post955393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is essential. A lot of people come at these games with an urban fantasy mindset and the rules are going to fight them every step of the way, leading to a lot of suffering at the table and angry forum posts later. Being upfront about how every line is going to try its darndest to hammer home both personal horror and its unique themes is really going to help things along.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the rules were <i>fine</i>. The rules didn't do any of that.<br /> <br /> It's just... man, I'm <i>still</i> surprised that these are horror games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T23:22:40-07:00","id":955447,"title":"","content":"I don't think the horror comes from acting like you're Robin Hood.<br /> <br /> It comes from the King of England being a twisted creature made of woven dreams and rotting flesh that stole you from Earth to participate in its own unholy mockery of a crusade, ripping your life out from under you and never being able to go back to your loved ones because you're too afraid of the Sheriff of Nottingham coming after you to take you back.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T00:08:10-07:00","id":955458,"title":"","content":"Whatever you do, don't feel the need to give loads of sessions to your players so that they'll like them. It merely becomes a drain on your inspiration and if you do it too much, you'll be so burned out you can barely give any sessions anymore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T04:22:58-07:00","id":955515,"title":"","content":"Create a simple problem, with a simple but hard to achieve solution. Then obscure the the problem, so that the players have a sense of mystery that leads them to this recognizing the problem. A simple problem, layered with subtext, and obscured with mystery is easier to run than a very complex problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T05:27:00-07:00","id":955531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=955393#post955393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is essential. A lot of people come at these games with an urban fantasy mindset and the rules are going to fight them every step of the way, leading to a lot of suffering at the table and angry forum posts later. Being upfront about how every line is going to try its darndest to hammer home both personal horror and its unique themes is really going to help things along.</div> </div> </div> </div> Umm... the games ARE urban fantasy. You have supernatural elements in an urban envirionment. Anyways, how is the mindset of the games being urban fantasy somehow going to fight with the rules and lead to suffering? Are you confusing urban fantasy with high fantasy, akin to D&amp;D? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T05:29:20-07:00","id":955532,"title":"","content":"That the games aren't meant to be combat focused fight fests where every scene is gearing up to the next violent encounter. Too much DnD influence on my running / playing style.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6365-fumus","name":"Fumus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6365_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T07:13:58-07:00","id":955562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SaulottheGentle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=955458#post955458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Whatever you do, don't feel the need to give loads of sessions to your players so that they'll like them. It merely becomes a drain on your inspiration and if you do it too much, you'll be so burned out you can barely give any sessions anymore.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean, &quot;give loads of sessions&quot;?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T07:14:43-07:00","id":955563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=955531#post955531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Umm... the games ARE urban fantasy. You have supernatural elements in an urban envirionment. Anyways, how is the mindset of the games being urban fantasy somehow going to fight with the rules and lead to suffering? Are you confusing urban fantasy with high fantasy, akin to D&amp;D? </div> </div> </div> </div>Urban fantasy emphasis is on action in my experience. My favorite urban fantasy series is the Dresden Files, which focuses on investigation, excitement, and often combat with cool superpowers. Personal horror also focuses on investigation and mystery, just like urban fantasy. But in personal horror emotional tension and drama are the main emphasis instead of action, excitement and investigation. Combat in a horror game tends to be on sided. In urban fantasy someone wins and someone loses, but they usually get away more or less unscaved so they can fight in another story. In personal horror the loser loses big, and the winner rarely gets away unscaved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T08:12:00-07:00","id":955590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=955562#post955562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean, &quot;give loads of sessions&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in giving at least one per day almost everyday. Let's just say that this is abit of a personal story of mine and I borked out after two years of that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Currently Doing: Siren the Drowning (Fansplat Ressurection) <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/779860-siren-the-surfacing-nwod-abandoned-fangame-resurrection\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/m...e-resurrection</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9750-saulotthegentle","name":"SaulottheGentle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9750_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"453"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T08:38:27-07:00","id":955605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>K9ine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=955563#post955563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Urban fantasy emphasis is on action in my experience.</div> </div> </div> </div> We must read different stories, then. My favorite urban fantasy stories actually don't have a lot action in them, but rather focus on mysteries and romance primarily. If anything, I find Dresden to be too action-y.<br /> <br /> On a whim, I recently got a pair of urban fantasy stories about a werewolf and vampire in school, and it primarily focused on bullying, social cliques, and interpersonal relationships in general. The closest things to an &quot;action scene&quot; were a volley ball game and were the werefox was trying to run away (and hide) from a janitor during a stealth mission. It was a pair of really cute stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 08-22-2016, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T09:37:20-07:00","id":955647,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=955605#post955605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> We must read different stories, then. My favorite urban fantasy stories actually don't have a lot action in them, but rather focus on mysteries and romance primarily. If anything, I find Dresden to be too action-y.<br /> <br /> On a whim, I recently got a pair of urban fantasy stories about a werewolf and vampire in school, and it primarily focused on bullying, social cliques, and interpersonal relationships in general. The closest things to an &amp;quot;action scene&amp;quot; were a volley ball game and were the werefox was trying to run away (and hide) from a janitor during a stealth mission. It was a pair of really cute stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, different than mine but still focused on a different tone than horror.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:16:03-07:00","id":955663,"title":"","content":"Who said there wasn't personal horror still? Genres are not mutually exclusive affairs here. There was plenty of personal horror and drama in the stories - in fact, it was pretty much the same savage horror that Forsaken offered, and the same personal horror from Requiem involved in the stories. I could <i>very </i>easily translate this into a CofD game with all horror themes intact. <br /> <br /> Here's my contribution to the thread - Urban fantasy stories have <i>lots </i>of suggestions that you can use for a CofD game. Lots of these stories are a mix of romance, mystery, horror and fiction, with elements you can weave into good chronicles. Lots of them don't focus on action or combat, and they have plenty of stories that show lateral challenges instead of scaling power challenges. Reading lots of stories from your genre can help you design and fix stories you wouldn't think of on your own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:27:28-07:00","id":955675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=955663#post955663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Who said there wasn't personal horror still? Genres are not mutually exclusive affairs here. There was plenty of personal horror and drama in the stories - in fact, it was pretty much the same savage horror that Forsaken offered, and the same personal horror from Requiem involved in the stories. I could <i>very </i>easily translate this into a CofD game with all horror themes intact.<br /> <br /> Here's my contribution to the thread - Urban fantasy stories have <i>lots </i>of suggestions that you can use for a CofD game. Lots of these stories are a mix of romance, mystery, horror and fiction, with elements you can weave into good chronicles. Lots of them don't focus on action or combat, and they have plenty of stories that show lateral challenges instead of scaling power challenges. Reading lots of stories from your genre can help you design and fix stories you wouldn't think of on your own.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they use the same ingrediants, but different spices, thats all I'm saying. They are ment to entertain in different ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12094-k9ine","name":"K9ine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12094_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T10:40:40-07:00","id":955686,"title":"","content":"You don't have to do a monolithic, strictly full horror chronicle anyway. Mixing spices and moods, switching from one colour to another during play and being flexible can often enhance your stories in ways that focused, mono-horror may not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T11:20:58-07:00","id":955725,"title":"","content":"... but you still should remember they <i>are</i> horror stories, in the end. I have my personal rule as ST:<br /> <br /> '<i>If do not know what to do with CoD game - just make it run for now as horror story.</i>'<br /> <br /> Even reality altering mages are better suited when one of them unfolds as soul sucking bastard / demon worshiper / simple bigot using cosmic powers to make people suffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:27:00-07:00","id":955845,"title":"","content":"My starting advice, don't forget that the world of darkness is a reflection of the real world. If your chronicle takes place in Tokyo then look at the real world Tokyo for ideas. Newspaper articles, history books, culture, all can be mined for ideas even if it's only an interesting backdrop like having your story take place during the 2020 Olympics. A chase is far more interesting if it's done while dodging through crowds of celebrants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-22T13:43:50-07:00","id":955859,"title":"","content":"List of names of NPCs with brief descriptions, things they want and have to offer. Annoying needing to come up with a name on the fly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T15:36:59-07:00","id":961268,"title":"","content":"All fantastic notes everyone (sorry, RL kept me busy).<br /> <br /> Another thing is, I don't think it was listed, but I like to go for the cool factor vs. reality. Whether it be a mechanic or a character. If I need an NPC to seem like a badass, I forego normal character rules. I will give him abilities from VtM because they look cool (thinking of Dementation where you would cause little hobgoblins to attack people based off their willpower). If I need a mechanic to do something that it normally doesn't, then oh well, it does now (i.e. vampires being infected by a disease and spreading it via feeding).<br /> <br /> In my stories, rule of cool &gt; realism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T17:45:58-07:00","id":961309,"title":"","content":"I actually try to avoid rules breaking by NPCs as often as possible. I might be biased, but it always annoyed me as a player and made me roll my eyes; so when I GM, I do my best to maintain both mechanical and story coherence, even if it sometimes reduces the cool factor. I value the fact that my players know that if an ability works in Way A, it will work in that way both for them and for NPCs, unless something specific modifies it. So I guess it's important to check if your players are ok with something like this before doing so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T21:21:46-07:00","id":961423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/954864-things-you-wish-you-knew-from-the-start?p=961309#post961309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually try to avoid rules breaking by NPCs as often as possible. I might be biased, but it always annoyed me as a player and made me roll my eyes; so when I GM, I do my best to maintain both mechanical and story coherence, even if it sometimes reduces the cool factor. I value the fact that my players know that if an ability works in Way A, it will work in that way both for them and for NPCs, unless something specific modifies it. So I guess it's important to check if your players are ok with something like this before doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the personalities of my players, yeah, I try as much as possible to keep to the rules and ensure that what applies for an NPC also runs true for a PC. Demon had some pretty serious culture shock in that respect with Interlocks meaning any NPC could have some special unique power unavailable to anyone else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-01T02:31:41-07:00","id":961539,"title":"","content":"Primary reason why we decided to not play Demon was it's attitude of &quot;I don't know, come up with something&quot; and &quot;It works when you think it's cool to work and it doesn't work when you think it's not cool to work&quot; when it came to their special powers, yes. But in general we dislike games that handle narrative power to players - it might be little conservative, but from where we stand, players should be players and GM should be GM; breaking this loses immersion for the players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}